    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0662" n="348" xml:id="pg348"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/1372</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-11-20">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 20, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>1104. Your 562, November 18. While waiting for full statement of facts about ship
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Uller</hi>, Sir Edward
                        Grey informs me that she was not detained because of cotton
                    cargo. Cotton is not stopped by Admiralty and will not be.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
